 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection in MATLAB, you need to add the gaussian filtering step before applying the Sobel operators. Here's the modified code:
```
input_image = imread('image.jpg'); % Read input image
% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Define Gaussian filter (standard deviation 1)
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [3 3], 1);
% Apply Gaussian filter
smoothed_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter);
% Define Sobel operator in x direction
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
% Define Sobel operator in y direction
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(smoothed_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(smoothed_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display original image, smoothed image, and edge image
subplot(1,3,1), imshow(input_image), title('Original Image');
subplot(1,3,2), imshow(smoothed_image), title('Smoothed Image');
subplot(1,3,3), imshow(edge_image), title('Edge Image');
```
This code applies a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial()` function and the `imfilter()` function before applying the Sobel edge detection to the input image. The standard deviation of the Gaussian filter is set to 1, but you can adjust it according to your requirements.

