 I see you've written a code snippet in JavaScript that iterates through an object `notifObj` containing notifications with different types and messages. In each iteration, it extracts the notification type `notifType` and its corresponding message `message`, and then returns an object with those properties.

To make this code more helpful and verbose, we can add some comments explaining what the code does and provide additional context. Here's the improved version:

```javascript
// Iterate through each entry in the notifications object
for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(notifObj)) {
  // Extract the notification type and message from the current entry
  const [notifType, notifArr] = value;
  const message = notifArr[0].message;

  // Create and return an object containing the notification type and message
  return {
    notifType, // The type of the notification
    message // The actual content of the notification
  };
}
```

